# Kaiser Jagdstandbild (Bad Ischl, 1910): the old emperor in hunting dress,
# a 24 px bronze figure O/l with a k outline (front layer): Tyrolean hat
# with a chamois-beard tuft t, Franz Joseph's whiskers (2x3 o mutton-chops
# on both cheeks joined by a 1 px o moustache), a Joppe O/l with t patina
# accents, Lederhosen O/l, knee socks t/T, boots l, a rifle l slung over
# his right shoulder. He stands on the 32x32 rough-hewn stone block (no k:
# i top lip rows 24-25, i lit left face and i/m left column, m mid face,
# d shadowed right face, right column and bottom rows, d chisel seams, a
# blank bronze plaque O/o/l: no text). Drawn = solid (D-038): the block is
# sprite rows 24..55 = the 2x2 stone tiles; its top is 32 px above the
# street. Pigeon seat (taube_sitting): the hat crown's top, pixels
# (14..18, 0), centred on the origin column x 16, 56 px above the street
# (24 px above the block).
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = kaiser_jagdstandbild
size   = 32x56
origin = 16,56
anim   = idle frames=1
